WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.502
Hello. Thank you so much.
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:07.273
My name is Mary Beth,
and I am actually living proof

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:10.243
that even self-aware
white people are terrible.

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:15.181
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:18.551
'Cause it's 2021.
People are getting woke, right?

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.954
And I'm from Connecticut,
I come from a great family,

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:23.590
so I'm, like, constantly
checking my privilege.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:24.957
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.726
To make sure it's still there.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:33.366
'Cause they keep trying to
take it, and I'm like, "No."

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.569
I need that, actually."

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:40.639
My family isn't wealthy.
We are comfortable.

00:00:40.639 --> 00:00:43.809
So, how I describe it is,
we do belong to a yacht club,

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:45.712
but we don't own a yacht.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.817
Or another way
of thinking about it --

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.752
I don't have
a trust fund to inherit,

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.655
but I was grandfathered
into unlimited data.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.524
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:03.263
My parents are super-supportive
of my comedy, especially my dad,

00:01:03.263 --> 00:01:05.631
'cause he did standup
back in the '70s,

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:08.902
and then he took the easy way
out and became a surgeon.

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.470
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:12.872
So I guess you could say

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.308
we're both in the business
of saving lives.

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.210
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.583
My mom's just happy
I didn't end up in a career

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:26.619
that would embarrass
the family...

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:29.288
like being a serial killer.

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:31.224
Or a venture capitalist.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.759
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.828
And they had six kids,
my mom and dad.

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:38.698
Now there's grandkids,
and I love my nieces,

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.967
but I do have beef
with my one nephew.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.968
He's 6 years old.

00:01:42.968 --> 00:01:45.671
And the other day,
he asked my sister-in-law --

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:48.875
He said, "Is Mary Beth
my aunt or my cousin?"

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.943
And she said,
"Mary Beth is your aunt."

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:52.745
And he said, "Well, then,
why does she always act

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.113
like a child?"

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:56.416
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.851
Which I thought was pretty rude.

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.120
So I ran and told my mom
he was bullying me

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.755
and got him in trouble.

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.223
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:07.960
[ Applause ]

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.828
I love kids. I really do.

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:12.332
I love kids so much,
I'm not going to have any.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.933
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:16.669
And whenever I say that,
the response is always the same.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:19.204
People tell me, "You're
going to change your mind.

00:02:19.204 --> 00:02:21.040
You're going to
change your mind 'cause if you

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.941
never have kids,
you'll never know what it's like

00:02:22.941 --> 00:02:26.178
to love someone
more than you love yourself."

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:28.748
And I was like,
"No, that's exactly my point."

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:30.549
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:35.020
That would be ideal, actually.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.089
I don't have time for kids
anyway.

00:02:37.089 --> 00:02:39.759
I have my hands full.
I'm dating a 27-year-old.

00:02:39.759 --> 00:02:41.561
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:44.230
And we met online.
He lives in England.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.432
So this definitely
was not part of my plan.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.768
I always thought
if I was going to date a guy,

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:50.336
he'd be really old.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:53.506
Like on death's door.
40 or something.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:56.141
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.141 --> 00:02:58.744
And I just feel like dating
an old guy would be really chill

00:02:58.744 --> 00:03:01.881
'cause they're too tired
to do anything...

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.950
and the font on their phone
is so big,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.852
you can read all their texts.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.487
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:10.022
[ Applause ]

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:13.226
I thought of that joke when
I was at dinner with my dad.

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:15.928
But he's married.

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:17.830
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.302
The guy I'm dating
is fully British,

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:26.172
so there's obviously
a language barrier.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:27.640
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.643
I've been taking classes,
which have been really helpful.

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:33.546
Because up until now, all of
my British cultural references

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:37.550
were what I learned
from the Spice Girls movie.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.553
Turns out England
has a rich history

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:44.356
of girl groups
I never even knew about.

00:03:44.356 --> 00:03:46.659
And things are going well,
but I don't know.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:49.261
We're just, like, at
different points in our lives.

00:03:49.261 --> 00:03:51.397
'Cause he's five hours ahead.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.698
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:54.733
If you're watching this, baby,
go to bed.

00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:58.104
It's 4 in the morning.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.306
International travel
is suspended right now,

00:04:00.306 --> 00:04:02.408
so he's not allowed
to come here,

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.276
and I know, like,
the virus and all that,

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:07.779
but it's annoying,
'cause he's wonderful.

00:04:07.779 --> 00:04:10.349
And I just know that I've been
romantically involved

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:11.850
with several people I legally

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.520
shouldn't have
been allowed to see.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.757
The guy who ran marathons
comes to mind.

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:21.760
Or the guy whose favorite band
was The Beatles.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.129
Or how about the guy
who texted me two summers ago

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:27.633
at 3 in the morning,
"What you up to?"

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:30.937
Where were you then,
federal government?

00:04:30.937 --> 00:04:32.438
You didn't want to intervene

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:35.842
when I took a $60 Uber
to Brooklyn?

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:39.178
Slept in a bed with
navy-blue sheets and one pillow?

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:42.348
Where -- Where were you?

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:45.518
But that's all behind me now,
and I'm so happy,

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:48.120
because after years of
hooking up with comedians,

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.723
I finally found a guy
with a real job.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.959
He's an actor.

00:04:52.959 --> 00:04:55.428
Thank you, guys, so much.
I'm Mary Beth.

